Same unsoundness as `$ZodPropertiesInternals` — the intersected type should be the input side, since nothing is written back onto the instance:

```ts
class Widget { tag?: string }
const W = z.instanceof(Widget).properties({ tag: z.string().default("none") });
const w = W.parse(new Widget());
w === input;  // true (identity preserved, as designed)
w.tag;        // type: string   actual: undefined
```

Also reachable through `.and()`.

`generatePropertiesChecks` emits no null guard, so the compiled check role throws where the interpreter reports an issue:

```ts
const s = z.any().check(...z.properties({ a: z.string() }));
s.safeParse(null);             // { code: "invalid_type", path: [] }
z.compile(s).safeParse(null);  // TypeError: Cannot read properties of null (reading 'a')
```

